 16:14:01)  [GCC 8.3.0]\r\n                     platform: Linux-5.4.0-42-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.27\r\n     optional deps. installed: ['typing-extensions']\r\n```\r\n<!-- or if you're using pydantic prior to v1.3, manually include: OS, python version and pydantic version -->\r\n\r\n<!-- Please read the [docs](https://pydantic-docs.helpmanual.io/) and search through issues to\r\nconfirm your bug hasn't already been reported. -->\r\n\r\n<!-- Where possible please include a self-contained code snippet describing your bug: -->\r\n\r\n```py\r\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\r\n\r\nclass SomeModel(BaseModel):\r\n    type: str = Field('set', const=True)\r\n    value: str\r\n\r\ndef try_parse(json_statham):\r\n    try:\r\n        SomeModel.parse_obj(json_statham)\r\n        print('success')\r\n    except ValueError:\r\n        print('cannot parse')\r\n\r\ntry_parse({'type': 'set', 'value': 'some value'})\r\ntry_parse({'type': 'lol', 'value': 'some value'})\r\ntry_parse({'value': 'some value'})\r\n```\r\nThe result will be:\r\n```\r\nsuccess\r\ncannot parse\r\nsuccess\r\n```\r\nIt looks pretty strange, I expect the last one will be `cannot parse` because field 'type' is **required** and I provide no value. Doc says:\r\n```\r\n:param const: this field is required and *must* take it's default value\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere is a workaround:\r\n```py\r\nfrom typing import Literal\r\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\r\n\r\nclass SomeModel(BaseModel):\r\n    type: Literal['set']\r\n    value: str\r\n```\r\nbut first example looks like bug.","closed_by":{"login":"dmontagu","id":35119617,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTE5NjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35119617?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu","html_url":"https://github.com/dmontagu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontag